WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.953
Oh my God, what is that?

00:00:00.953 --> 00:00:03.620
This is a black-throated monitor lizard.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.990
Okay, where do you want me for this?

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.617
Can I be in a cage of some kind?

00:00:06.617 --> 00:00:07.810
No, you don't have to be in a cage.

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:09.780
Now, this guy's name is Darth Vader,

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.750
and he's pretty aptly named
because when he gets upset

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.930
he starts to hiss and moan
just like Darth Vader would.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.860
Darth Vader doesn't moan.
(audience laughing)

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:21.664
He doesn't hiss or moan.
Yeah, he does.

00:00:21.664 --> 00:00:24.487
Oh, Luke!
Listen, if you saw--

00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:26.213
(Conan moaning)

00:00:26.213 --> 00:00:28.335
If you saw "Revenge of the
Sith" he moans at the end.

00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:30.870
He doesn't really moan.
(audience applauding)

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.873
So anyway, this guys lives in Africa.

00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:34.405
Can I put my hand out or is
that the dumbest thing to do?

00:00:34.405 --> 00:00:35.980
You know what, you can
pet him on the back here,

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.330
but you probably want to keep
your hand away from his mouth.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.776
I'm going up over your head.

00:00:38.776 --> 00:00:39.800
There you go, you can do that.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.660
I'm using your skull as protection.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.820
You're tall enough, so...

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.980
Okay, so this, yes.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.807
So anyways, this is a
large carnivorous lizard.

00:00:46.807 --> 00:00:50.070
Oh, look at him, he's looking
around like, that felt good.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.410
He probably smells the cavy,

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:55.390
which is an animal about
the size that he would eat.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.330
These guys like to eat small
mammals just like that rodent.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.860
Is there anything I can feed

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:01.180
this monitor lizard right now?

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.700
You know, actually nope.
Oh.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.701
We're not gonna feed him

00:01:03.701 --> 00:01:07.020
because if you get him stimulated--

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.160
If you feed him he's
happy and doesn't attack.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.650
He might try to eat me.
Yeah, all right.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:11.860
But yeah, check out those huge claws,

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.110
the tongue sticking out.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.570
People think you get stung by that,

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.010
but it's actually how they smell.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.110
It's just like a snake.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.450
They collect scent particles
and bring them back

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.340
into their mouth and that's
how they kind of figure out

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.370
what's going on in their environment.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:23.910
So this, not a good candidate

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.510
for making chums with another species.

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.270
He'll just kill anything,
he's a creep, yeah.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.160
Exactly, exactly, well, you
know, predators, you know,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.020
they get a bad rap because
they eat other animals,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.300
but they're really important.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.040
You know, conservation-wise
we want to protect them.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:36.570
But yeah, if we brought out
one of the little furry guys

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.800
with this lizard, wouldn't last very long.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.090
Right, okay.
Yeah.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:41.560
Sounds like a good segment to me.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.012
Yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:01:43.012 --> 00:01:44.630
We're about protecting the wildlife.

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:45.680
Yeah, I think you're not understanding

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.740
how television works.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.730
If we put these next two species together,

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.890
they'd fight to death,
but let's not see that.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.040
All right, so our last species here

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.010
is really, really cool.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.240
It's actually the first
time that I've worked

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.410
with this particular species.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:02.350
It's called an African
southern ground hornbill.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.520
And he's taking his time coming in.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:05.595
[Conan] Doesn't seem to want to come in.

00:02:05.595 --> 00:02:09.345
(Andy and audience laughing)

00:02:12.454 --> 00:02:14.910
Did he run the other way?
He just, I love that.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.586
He took one peek and he
was like, I think not.

00:02:17.586 --> 00:02:19.090
(audience laughing)

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.480
Come on, it's a fun show.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.900
Don't go by what you've read.
(audience laughing)

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.194
What is this, tell me, this
is a fascinating looking bird.

00:02:27.194 --> 00:02:28.770
Okay, yeah, it's a bird, right.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:32.150
It's called a southern
ground hornbill, okay.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:33.490
When you look at an animal like this

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:37.460
you can really see how birds
are descended from dinosaurs.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.760
Let's see if we can get him over here now.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.040
Now Conan, I'm gonna give you,

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:43.435
do you want a piece of fruit
or a chunk of dead mouse?

00:02:43.435 --> 00:02:46.050
(audience groans)
I would say neither.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.570
Okay.
(audience laughing)

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:48.540
[Conan] I'll have neither one.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.020
Is it really, you just
put a mouse in a blender?

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:54.330
Well, you know, you buy them frozen

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:57.233
and it's for carnivorous animals.

00:02:57.233 --> 00:02:58.429
Look at that.
Anyway, these guys

00:02:58.429 --> 00:02:59.700
are carnivores, they're
actually omnivores,

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.500
but they're out hunting
in the African savanna.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.960
And they're looking, check out those eyes.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.930
They're really huge eyes
with really long eyelashes.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.487
Boink.
Yeah, that didn't work.

00:03:09.487 --> 00:03:12.260
Huge eyes that didn't see
the huge clump of dead mouse

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.270
coming his way.
(audience laughing)

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:17.090
And then what is that thing
on the front of its throat?

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.140
[Trainer] So that helps them vocalize.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.550
They're social birds, you
can hear him making all sorts

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.383
of little squeaks and--

00:03:21.383 --> 00:03:22.869
Yeah, he sounds just like Darth Vader.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.869
(audience laughing)

00:03:26.912 --> 00:03:30.077
(Conan mimics bird)
Come on, we're friends.

00:03:30.077 --> 00:03:31.660
[Trainer] Yeah, I walked in to that one.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.270
So check out the bill here.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.204
Southern hornbill is
the name of the species.

00:03:36.204 --> 00:03:38.870
That bill is strong enough
that it could actually

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:41.180
crack through the shell of a tortoise.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.690
Really?
They have a fused vertebrate

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:44.000
in their neck and they can pound you,

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.730
which is why we're not
getting any closer to him

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.120
because he's--
He's pretty close.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.600
Well, you know, if you tried
to pick him up right now.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.433
Yeah.
He could actually,

00:03:51.433 --> 00:03:54.180
like, break a bone in your hand
if he nailed you with that.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.980
Well, I have very weak bones
so that's not saying a lot.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.483
I really do, I'm just terribly weak bones.

00:04:00.343 --> 00:04:01.850
A little chunk of dead mouse.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.510
I can't get over the chunks of dead mouse.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.560
That's freaking me out right now.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.393
Well, you know what?

00:04:05.393 --> 00:04:06.970
When you take care of
these animals in captivity

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.590
you gotta feed 'em what
is healthy for them,

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:10.020
and in this case that's what they eat.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.840
They eat other small animals.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.673
[Conan] Well, I've noticed

00:04:12.673 --> 00:04:14.600
you never come on the
show with a mouse, so...

